Subject: audiomgr: make the "plenty queued" throttle a port-settable threshold

amgrFrame() renders 368 samples per 60 Hz tick — unless the audio queue
already holds more than 1100 samples, in which case it renders 184 and sets a
two-tick hysteresis counter. That governor is an N64 AI-queue heuristic and it
predates anything that controls the queue level deliberately.

This port does control it. D-039's rate matcher holds the queue at one and a
half DEVICE buffers, and on iOS the device buffer is floored at 1024 samples
(overlay 0023, M-029), so the setpoint is **1536 — permanently above 1100**.
The engine therefore throttles for ever: 184, 368, 368, 184, … averaging about
306 samples a tick where 367 are consumed, a 17 % production deficit that no
PI loop can close, which is why `audio_rate_milli` sat pinned at its +10 %
clamp (Q-017, D-042). The clamp was covering a governor fighting the
controller, not a clock.

It is not a 120 Hz problem, which is where it was first seen: schedAudioFrame()
runs amgrFrame() once per 60 Hz tick (`g_Vars.diffframe60`) at any render rate,
so the deficit is the same at 60. 120 only made it audible.

So the threshold becomes a variable rather than a literal, and on iOS it is
raised above the setpoint: the engine always renders its full 368 per tick and
the rate matcher is the only thing deciding how fast those samples reach the
device — one controller, not two. Every other platform keeps 1100 and nothing
changes. Production is 22,080 samples/s against 22,851 consumed (M-036), i.e.
BELOW consumption, so the queue cannot run away with the governor raised, and
`queueLimit` (16384 on iOS) is still the hard ceiling.

diff --git a/port/src/audio.c b/port/src/audio.c
index 63ed859b0..0b456cf27 100644
--- a/port/src/audio.c
+++ b/port/src/audio.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include "audio.h"
 #include "record.h"
 #include "system.h"
+#include "lib/audiomgr.h"   /* g_AmgrThrottleSamples (overlay 0028) */
 
 static SDL_AudioDeviceID dev;
 static const s16 *nextBuf;
@@ -637,5 +638,9 @@ PD_CONSTRUCTOR static void audioConfigInit(void)
 	configRegisterInt("Audio.PrimeSamples", &primeSamples, 0, 32 * 1024);
 	configRegisterInt("Audio.RateMatch", &rateMatch, 0, 1);
 	configRegisterInt("Audio.RateMatchMaxPct", &rateMatchMaxPct, 0, PD_AUDIO_RATE_MAX_PCT);
+	// The ENGINE's own governor (overlay 0028, D-042), exposed so the pair can
+	// be A/B'd live on the phone: set it to 1100 and amgrFrame() goes back to
+	// throttling itself to 184 samples on alternate ticks.
+	configRegisterInt("Audio.EngineThrottleSamples", &g_AmgrThrottleSamples, 0, 1 * 1024 * 1024);
 #endif
 }
diff --git a/src/include/lib/audiomgr.h b/src/include/lib/audiomgr.h
